        {
          "id": "a352727a-d391-49f0-956e-948f85ad2c3e",
          "name": "Sign-In with Auto Sign-up",
          "request": {
            "name": "Sign-In with Auto Sign-up",
            "description": {
              "content": "### Sign-in end user (with automatic sign-up) by sending an OTP code via Voice\nInitiate a process that implements both sign-in and sign-up using a single endpoint. Descope will generate and deliver the One-Time Password (OTP) to the end user via Voice. If the phone number is already registered (the end user exists) the user will be signed in. If the phone number is not registered (the end user is not yet registered) the user will be signed up. Sending multiple OTP codes (for example, when an end user tries to sign-up/sign-in a second or third time) will invalidate any OTP code that has already been sent.\n\nThis endpoint will return an empty response object when it completes successfully.\n\n### Next Steps\nVerify the OTP code using the [Verify OTP Code](/api/otp/phone/verify-otp) endpoint to complete the user sign-in process.\nAfter successfully verifying the code the end user will be signed-in.\n\n### See Also\n- See [The User Object](/api/overview#the-user-object) for further details on how to identify users and their contact information such as email address and phone number.\n- See [User Login Options](/api/overview#user-login-options) for further details on loginOptions.\n- Use the [Sign-Up](/api/otp/phone/sign-up) endpoint if you want a sign-up flow that will fail if the end user is already registered.\n- Use the [Sign-In](/api/otp/phone/sign-in-auto-sign-up) endpoint if you want a sign-in flow that will fail if the end user isn't yet registered.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "otp",
                "signup-in",
                "voice"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
